        "original_id": "b4653542-aea9-59b9-bb7f-90441e0b2c11",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City, Madison Avenue, East 23rd Street, Madison Square Park, Chelsea, Hell's Kitchen, Penn Station area, Venice, Italy\n- Buildings: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, 15 Hudson Yards, Campanile in Venice\n- Companies: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company, Hedden Construction Company\n- Organizations: Metropolitan Transportation Authority\n- Projects: Hudson Yards project, West Side Yards redevelopment\n- People: Napoleon LeBrun & Sons\n\nFacts:\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower is a landmark skyscraper on Madison Avenue near East 23rd Street, across from Madison Square Park in Manhattan, New York City.\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower is colloquially known as the Met Life Tower.\n- Napoleon LeBrun & Sons designed the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, and the Hedden Construction Company built it.\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower was modeled after the Campanile in Venice, Italy.\n- 15 Hudson Yards is located in Chelsea near the Hell's Kitchen Penn Station area.\n- 15 Hudson Yards is part of the Hudson Yards project to redevelop the Metropolitan Transportation Authority's West Side Yards.",
